From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ad5xrecon <ad5xrecon@localhost>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 16:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] sound: sysfs PWM speaker on MIPS, printer sounds in Sound

The unified MIPS build (PLATFORM_TARGET=mips) now carries the sysfs PWM
sound backend. AD5X OS's kernel exposes the speaker as a pwmchip channel
and its start script names it with HELIX_PWM_SOUND=0:13 only when the
speaker is there; a named channel wins over every other backend. Without
one nothing probes sysfs PWM on this platform (no HELIX_PWM_AUTO_EXPORT),
so the stock kernel keeps the jz_pwm path. The backend writes only
export, period, duty_cycle and enable, never polarity.

Settings > Sound gets a "Printer Sounds" section, shown only where Klipper
has the ad5x_sound object and found a speaker: an on/off switch, the
volume (sent when the slider is released) and one row per print event
with the sound it plays (Off or one of the printer's sound files) and a
button that plays it. Every change is a SOUND_SETUP command, the play
button PLAY_SOUND. The object joins the status subscription; the controls
follow it, except one being changed and while a change is unanswered.

Upstream: not applicable (AD5X OS specific)
